{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"antihuman-beefwitted-zebra","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nGerrit intermittently fails to serve git fetches, returning **HTTP 504** and killing CI checkouts\nbefore any test runs. It is currently blocking changes across multiple concurrent sessions.\n\n## PROVEN — a homogeneous failure class\n\nAmong today's last 40 `Gerrit Verified Gate` runs, FOUR failed in the checkout step\n(`require resolvable rebar ticket`). **All four carry the identical signature:**\n\n```\nrun 33995047786  change 2684 PS2   7x HTTP 504 | 7x RPC failed | 2x expected 'packfile'\nrun 33994272323  change 2686 PS1      HTTP 504 | RPC failed    | expected 'packfile'\nrun 33975450189  change 2680 PS1      HTTP 504 | RPC failed    | expected 'packfile'\nrun 33975439688  change 2666 PS9      HTTP 504 | RPC failed    | expected 'packfile'\n```\n\n4 of 4 — not a sample, the whole class. Two occurred within one hour of each other on changes\nowned by DIFFERENT sessions, so this is not one session's misconfiguration.\n\n## PROVEN — corroboration from three other vantage points, same window\n\n- `Mirror Guard` runs 33990613226 (20:36Z) and 33991235523 (20:49Z) failed with\n  `{\"check\":\"io\",\"healthy\":false,\"reason\":\"fetch error: <urlopen error _ssl.c:993: The handshake\n  operation timed out>\"}` — while the mirror was VERIFIABLY IN SYNC (Gerrit and GitHub `main` both\n  at `4c9940348148`). The guard could not reach the host; nothing had diverged.\n- A `curl` to the Gerrit REST API from a developer host returned an empty body with no HTTP code,\n  and succeeded on immediate retry.\n- A `git fetch` from the `gerrit` remote returned HTTP 504 and succeeded on retry.\n\nFive independent observations, four distinct clients (GitHub Actions runner, GitHub Actions\ncheckout action, developer curl, developer git), one host.\n\n## CORRECTION to an earlier framing — do not repeat it\n\n`Gerrit Verified Gate` shows 20 of 36 completed runs failing today (55%), which looks like a\ncatastrophic gate. **It is NOT all this bug.** Partitioned by failing job:\n\n```\noptionality (lean-runtime + packaging)   10   the terraform-config-inspect canary bug,\n                                              root-caused and FIXED earlier today (2678/2676/2677)\nrequire resolvable rebar ticket           4   THIS BUG\nbuild-and-test                            5   includes one CANCELLATION (2683 PS2, superseded)\n                                              and genuine test failures\nverify-identity                           1   one-off\n```\n\nThe headline 55% is dominated by an already-fixed defect. Anyone citing it as evidence for this\nbug is over-attributing — I nearly did.\n\n## HYPOTHESIS — a LEAD, explicitly NOT established\n\nA 504 on a git fetch is a gateway timeout waiting for Gerrit to produce a packfile, which is\nCPU- and IO-intensive. The same host is under known IO pressure:\n\n- `/var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch` holds 9.3 GB on the ROOT filesystem because the dedicated EBS\n  volume was never formatted or mounted (`renowned-corked-hapuku` / dcc3), so review-gate snapshots\n  and per-review clones contend with the OS disk — the exact outage shape of bug 3276.\n- The observability probe is being SIGTERM-ed on its 4-minute timeout with only ~42 s of CPU\n  consumed, i.e. it is blocked on I/O (`ignitable-fuchsia-kawala` / 9313), and its tail metrics\n  have degraded to roughly 1 datapoint in 3 hours.\n\nSo \"IO saturation slows packfile generation past the proxy timeout\" is PLAUSIBLE and would link\nthree open tickets. It is NOT proven: no correlation has been established between 504 timestamps\nand host IO, and no proxy timeout value has been read. Do not fix on the strength of this\nparagraph — test it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 A falsifiable hypothesis for the 504s is stated, with the observation that would\n      disprove it, BEFORE any fix.\n- [ ] AC2 The mechanism is established by correlating 504 timestamps against host-side evidence\n      (Gerrit/httpd logs, proxy timeout configuration, host IO and CPU at those instants) — not by\n      plausibility. The IO hypothesis above must be confirmed or refuted explicitly.\n- [ ] AC3 If the cause is a proxy/gateway timeout that is simply too short for legitimate packfile\n      work, say so — raising it is then a fix, not a workaround. If instead the host cannot serve\n      in reasonable time, that is a capacity finding and needs a different remedy. Distinguish\n      them.\n- [ ] AC4 CI distinguishes a transport failure from a test verdict, so a 504 checkout does not\n      present as a change's failure. It currently reads as the change being broken; four changes\n      across three sessions were mislabelled today.\n- [ ] AC5 A measurable before/after rate is recorded, using the PARTITIONED counts above rather\n      than the raw 55%.\n\n## Constraints\n\nNever use `--force` or any gate bypass. `timeout` does not exist on this macOS host (exit 127) —\nbound with `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`. Terraform may be written and validated; applying is\noperator-authorized this session and must follow a reviewed plan. Do not touch the shared main\ncheckout; do not `git stash` anywhere.","id":"5bba-45dd-3bfc-42f1","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gerrit returns HTTP 504 on git fetch, breaking CI checkouts across sessions"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788646389354975001,"uuid":"73fc6b7b-8448-4878-a631-a6327c3f2887"}